    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="1065" n="907" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg907"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Italian
                    Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_apparent-typo-based-on-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                        1996</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 425.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In reply to your note of the 24th
                    ultimo, in the matter of the protest of S. Rae &amp; Co., of Leghorn, against
                    the alleged <pb facs="1066" n="908" xml:id="pg908"/> refusal of this Government
                    to admit Tuscan olive oil labeled as Lucca oil unless made in or exported from
                    Lucca, I have the honor to inclose a copy of a letter from the Secretary of
                    Agriculture stating the views of his department.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d37-a1.xml" xpointer="d37-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
